# 6. IMPORTANT BUSINESS CALCULATIONS

The application must clearly distinguish between:

### Gross Sales

Gross sales before deductions.

Example:

Gross Sales =
Quantity × Selling Price

### Discount

Discount given to customers.

### Net Sales

Net Sales =
Gross Sales - Discount

### Cost

Cost of goods sold.

### Profit

Profit =
Net Sales - Cost

### Loss

If Profit < 0:

Loss = absolute value of Profit

### Profit Margin

Profit Margin =
(Profit / Net Sales) × 100

### Average Order Value

AOV =
Net Sales / Number of Orders

### Return Rate

Return Rate =
Returned Orders / Total Orders × 100

or, when appropriate,

Returned Quantity / Sold Quantity × 100

Clearly identify which definition is being displayed.

